course: dictionary
lesson: 6125
title: Midnight and the clock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Midnight is twelve o'clock at night, the moment one day ends and the next one begins. «The shop closes at midnight» tells you the shop shuts at that moment, when one day turns into the next.
explain: On a 24-hour clock, midnight is 00:00 and noon is 12:00. From midnight to noon is 12 hours. «A night shift from 22:00 to 06:00» crosses midnight, so split it in two: 2 hours up to midnight plus 6 hours after it makes 8 hours.
explain: Midnight can also mean the middle of the night, a very late hour. «A boy in Ohio called Josh watched his tablet until midnight every school night» tells you it was very late, so late that he was falling asleep in class.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The family stayed up until twelve o'clock at night» still makes sense, so you know midnight means twelve o'clock at night.
fact: Midnight is written as 00:00 on the 24-hour clock, or as 12:00 a.m. on a normal clock.
fact: Noon, or midday, is 12:00 on the 24-hour clock, or 12:00 p.m. on a normal clock.
fact: «Kiritimati, an island in Kiribati, is 14 hours ahead of London» so when it is midnight there, it is still 10 am on the same date in London.
fact: «Burn the midnight oil» means to work late into the night.
fact: In the story of Cinderella, the magic ends at midnight.
exercise: On the 24-hour clock, what time is 00:00? | Noon | Half past twelve | Eleven at night | *Midnight
exercise: «The family stayed up past midnight.» How many hours are there from midnight to noon? | *12 | 10 | 6 | 24
exercise: «A night shift from 22:00 to 06:00» lasts how many hours? | 12 | 10 | *8 | 6
test: What does «burn the midnight oil» mean? | To go to a party | To light a candle | To sleep in until noon | *To work late into the night
test: Which time is the same as midnight on the 24-hour clock? | 22:00 | 06:00 | *00:00 | 12:30
exam: On New Year's Eve, a family «tries to stay up past midnight (shǒusuì)». What does past midnight mean here? | At noon | Before twelve o'clock at night | *After twelve o'clock at night | At six in the morning
